This PR is yet another attempt to add an ability for configure CSS loader options.

Previouses were PR #15810, RFC #15818 and some special cases related to it like PR #11276.

There are many reasons we might want to be able to add/change CSS loader options. The main option for me is [modules.exportLocalsConvention](https://webpack.js.org/loaders/css-loader/#exportlocalsconvention) which (by `camelCase` value) allows using dashes in CSS modules, but exports camel-cased classes to JS. Thanksful to this we can use shorter and prettier syntax `styles.listItemButton` instead of `styles['list-item-button']`.

Nuxt.js has these options in its configuration: https://nuxtjs.org/docs/2.x/configuration-glossary/configuration-build#loaders

