Accept arrays for `redirects`, `rewrites`, and `headers` in `next.config.js`. The vast majority of use cases don't require a function and from the people I've spoken to this is the generally expected behavior. Especially important since passing an array — as one might try to do — does not throw any kind of error or warning. Example of difference:

## Before
```js
module.exports = {
  redirects() {
    return [
      {
        source: '/hello-3',
        destination: '/world',
        permanent: false
      }
    ]
  },
  rewrites() {
    return [
      {
        source: '/hello-1',
        destination: '/world'
      }
    ]
  },
  headers() {
    return [
      {
        source: '/hello-3',
        headers: [
          {
            key: 'x-path',
            value: 'hello-3'
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

## After
```js
module.exports = {
  redirects: [
    {
      source: '/hello-1',
      destination: '/world',
      permanent: false
    }
  ],
  rewrites: [
    {
      source: '/hello-2',
      destination: '/world'
    }
  ],
  headers: [
    {
      source: '/hello-3',
      headers: [
        {
          key: 'x-path',
          value: 'hello-3'
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

