Interpolation failure of dynamic routes when the query parameter matches any of the slug patterns results in an uncatchable thrown Error. Instead, this Error should only be thrown when `process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'`. This allows the parameters to pass through to the various server side and client side functions/router and can be handled appropriately in userland.

As is, the Error that is thrown cannot be caught in any of the provided server side functions, nor with an `ErrorBoundary` that wraps the entire application. 

